{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/312685-advice","id":312685,"title":"Advice.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-14T18:14:10-08:00","id":312685,"title":"Advice.","content":"Hi there I was wondering if you could give me some advice as to how to run an X-men like game within the setting of aberrant and adventure. I have read both core books and as far as I can tell in adventure people don't believe in extraordinary humans and in aberrant they are celebrities. How would you fit a group of outcasts with superpowers in these settings?. Yes I know you can always change the setting to your liking but I would like to keep them both as intact as possible. Any suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 11-15-2014, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T06:06:36-08:00","id":312888,"title":"","content":"It's easier to do in <b>Aberrant</b>, where it's mostly a matter of tone being different. Novas are often celebrities but not 100% trusted by baseline humanity. The Aberrants form an underground group on the run from a secret agency with an anti-Nova agenda. The Teragen speak for Nova separatism or supremacy and plenty of them act like the Brotherhood of Evil Mutants, the Church of Michael Archangel is one example of an anti-Nova group in human society, ReignOfEvil is a modern wannabe Hellfire Club. The timeline advances in the <b>Aberrant Worldwide</b> adventures to a point where conflict between baseline humanity and the Novas is all but certain.<br /> <br /> In rules terms I'd consider lowering starting Nova Points, as a &quot;normal&quot; starting Nova is pretty powerful by <b>X-Men</b> standards and so less likely to work semi-subtly than the X-Men have to.<br /> <br /> Another alternative which fits the current canon would be a &quot;prequel&quot; like <b>X-Men: First Class</b>, with a smaller number of <b><i>Adventure!</i></b> level characters operating in secret in the gap between the end of the <b><i>Adventure!</i></b> era and the beginning of the <b>Aberrant</b> era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T16:04:50-08:00","id":313333,"title":"","content":"Thanks for answer, if you don't mind I have a couple of questions have you planned any other eras? Is there any possibility that we would see a Victoria era supplement? Like league of extraordinary gentleman? and how about world war one, world war 2 and cold war?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T18:01:27-08:00","id":313378,"title":"","content":"Hey Firanai.<br /> <br /> At the moment, the only announced eras are Aeon (2120s), Aberrant ('day after tomorrow'), Adventure! (1920s) and the 'modern' setting that comes with the core rulebook. There's been hints about other settings being planned but nothing announced <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T18:35:15-08:00","id":313385,"title":"","content":"oh well, It will have to do for now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T12:34:28-08:00","id":313896,"title":"","content":"It seems that the plan is definitely to expand the Continuum further than those three lines, I assume depending upon how well sales go of the rest. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T14:35:00-08:00","id":313980,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I have every intention of doing a Days of Future Past storyline at some point with events in one &quot;timezone&quot; affecting the story in other &quot;timezones&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T21:49:56-08:00","id":314203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/312685-advice?p=313980#post313980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I have every intention of doing a Days of Future Past storyline at some point with events in one &quot;timezone&quot; affecting the story in other &quot;timezones&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I have done one vaguely similar to that linking Aberrant and Aeon, it took a few false starts (but that was not the fault of the concept really) and was fun once it got going on both ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T23:52:04-08:00","id":314295,"title":"","content":"I have done the whole Adventure! character that lives to Aberrant and then survives all the way to Trinity (Thank you Optimized Metabolism) but I wanted to toy with the villain finally being revealed in Aeon with Aberrant showing it's rise to power and then in Adventure! showing how it was first formed.<br /> Then I heard that they had no less than 7 different time settings and the ideas exploded about what could be done. I am itching to find out what those will be to see if they can be added in.<br /> But, getting back to the OP of this thread, it is easy to do X-Men if you remember the basic premise of X-Men, namely they protect a world that hates and fears them. Mechanics-wise? Stay the same with Aberrant. Just alter the setting and not let them be celebrities at all. When it comes to doing it with Adventure!, you would simply have them run as an early Hellfire Club (if you are familiar with X-Men lore) and then move that forward to letting the new Black King/Queen and White King/Queen and end up with them being novas in the modern day and age. Not to mention, in the comics, Xavier and Magneto were not kids during WW II (but those stories were also done in the 80's) and so you could also run those kinds of stories with your mutants running from the nazis.<br /> Just throwing out ideas for how to run X-Men style stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}